{
  "about": "The requirement of quoteOneLine (machinery#32): quote an untrusted string for one-line terminal output. It guarantees one line with no raw control (Cc), format (Cf), line separator (Zl), paragraph separator (Zp) or lone surrogate. It is not ASCII-only: every other code point, such as e acute, an emoji or U+00A0, is left as it is. The cases hold from Unicode 15 on; an implementation follows its own Unicode version, which may escape later format characters. Each case's input is a list of code points (a value in U+D800..U+DFFF is a lone surrogate); output is the exact result.",
  "rule": [
    "Keep the first max code points of the value (default 40); a surrogate pair is one code point and is never split, a lone surrogate is one.",
    "Apply JSON.stringify: quotes, backslash, C0 controls and lone surrogates are escaped as JSON does (\\b \\t \\n \\f \\r, or lower-case \\u00xx and \\udxxx).",
    "Then write every code point of general category Cc, Cf, Zl or Zp that is still raw as \\uxxxx (lower-case, four digits) or, above U+FFFF, \\u{x} (lower-case, no padding).",
    "Every other code point is left as it is."
  ],
